Multi Container pods cannot be executed using imperative commands, We will need to write yaml file. 
Multi container pods share the same network .

3 different types of multi container pods are - 

1 - Co-located Containers -They are run till the end of pod lifecycle. Challenge is we cannot decide which container will start first.  

2 - Init Containers - Init containers always run to complete, once the initi containers completes/Terminates the main app container runs. We can have multiple init containers, init containers will run once at a time in the order mentioned in yaml file . 

Starting of Main container completely depends on init Container. 

3 - Sidecar Containers / Helper Container - They are run till the end of pod lifecycle. It also uses init container but restart policy is set to Always which means both main container and sidecar containers will continue to run until pod lifecycle. 

If an init container is created with its restartPolicy set to Always, it will start and remain running during the entire life of the Pod. This can be helpful for running supporting services separated from the main application containers.

apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: colocatedcontainer
spec:
  containers:
  - name: check-google
    image: alpine/curl
    command: ["ping","-c","10","google.com"]
  - name: check-kubernetes
    image: alpine/curl
    command: ["curl","kubernetes.io"]


apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: initcontainer
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app-container
    image: nginx
  initContainers:
  - name: check-google
    image: alpine/curl
    command: ["ping","-c","10","google.com"]
  - name: check-kubernetes
    image: alpine/curl
    command: ["curl","kubernetes.io"]



apiVersion: v1
kind: Pod
metadata:
  name: side-carcontainer
spec:
  containers:
  - name: app-container
    image: nginx
  initContainers:
  - name: check-google
    image: alpine/curl
    command: ["ping","-c","10","google.com"]
    restartPolicy: Always. #### This is what makes init container in sidecar continues to run till end of pod lifecycle 


